/E (UNODC works to educate people throughout the world about the dangers of drug abuse and to strengthen international action against illicit drug production and trafficking and drug-related crime. To achieve those aims, UNODC has launched a range of initiatives, including alternatives in the area of illicit drug crop cultivation, monitoring of illicit crops and the implementation of projects against money laundering. These efforts demonstrate that combating drug trafficking requires more than simply stopping the physical movement of drugs. Financial investigations, prevention programs and international information sharing can also contribute to reducing the activities of criminal networks. )
/Pg 15 0 R
