/E ( The United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\) is the lead office to assist member states in their fight against illicit substance trafficking, transnational organised crime and acts of planned terrorism. UNODC was established in 1997 when the United Nations Drug Control Programme and the Centre for International Crime Prevention were merged. The headquarters of the establishment is located in Vienna, Austria. UNODC has approximately 500 staff members and it operates 20 field offices. As a result, UNODC plays an important role in helping countries address drug trafficking through international cooperation and shared strategies. Its work is especially relevant to emerging forms of drug trafficking that use digital platforms and modern technologies. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
