/E ( The emergence of the Dark Web has significantly affected the illicit drug trafficking market by providing criminals a platform to communicate anonymously and privately. The main reason that the dark web drug trade is such a threat is that unlike traditional ways that the criminals use they cannot be tracked as they leave almost no trace behind because the network is quite literally the most private part of the whole world wide web. Users typically access these networks through special specifically designed software, such as Tor \(The Onion Router\) which hides their identities andlocations by routing internet traffic through multiple encrypted layers. Even though the dark webonly takes up a small percentage of the whole world wide web, as it is less than one percent of it,itstill is quite dangerous and users who access it face great threats such as their data getting stolenorbeing subjected to a number of illegal activities that include the trafficking of drugs, illegalpornography or cases of homicide. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
