/E (pros and cons to the distributors.The first way is the usage of drug mules.A mule essentially is a courier, and serves the purpose of delivering the illicit drugs.Mules do not have to be the smugglers friend or ally and their relationship with the smuggler is in most cases can be observed to have some correlation with the type of drug they are delivering.Easy to replace drugs such as fentanyl do not need highly trustable mules but hard to replace expensive and valuable drugs such as heroin and cocaine usually are carried by mules that are at least on some level trusted by the distributor.The second and the more common way of transporting the drugs are postal services.The drugs are usually pretty well hidden within the contents of the sent package so often they are left unseen.Despite the advantages of having mules, postal systems remain the most popular way of transporting illicit drugs across nations. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
