/S /P
/P 233 0 R
/E ( One of the most frustrating challenges that law enforcement has to go through is the fact that taking down a big marketplace on the dark web has serious consequences. Once a large market is busted the customers and the vendors immediately start looking for and creating alternatives which in turn results in more marketplaces being created and the users spreading to different places. This has happened multiple times in the recorded history of the dark web with the most significant one being the takedown operation on the silk road which brought more eyes to the dark web as the takedown was talked about globally which in turn created more customers and vendors. This demonstrates that shutting down a single platform may not be enough to permanently reduce illegal activity. Law enforcement agencies must also consider how criminal networks reorganize themselves after major operations. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 233 0 R
/E (Cross nation agreements on the conditions and permissions on most scenarios takes some time toreach a conclusion. By the time a conclusive agreement is reached the digital evidence can be discarded or the suspects might have moved to another platform before any sort of meaningful action can be taken. Criminals on the internet move fast so any time wasted means a potential for them to get away with it. Establishing clearer international procedures could reduce delays and allow authorities to respond more effectively. Strengthening cooperation while respecting national laws and jurisdiction could make cross-border investigations more efficient. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
