/P 234 0 R
/E ( The topic of how far governments are willing to go in order to create a safe environment on the internet is a heavily debated topic especially in recent times with the surge in popularity of the dark web. Weakening encryption and anonymization tools in order to slow down criminals effects the people who are truly using it for innocent purposes such as journalism and activism. Governments must therefore consider whether new security measures could unintentionally harm legitimate users. Finding a balance between effective law enforcement and the protection of privacy remains an important challenge for the international community. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
