/E ( Encrypted messaging apps such as telegram offer true private chats with people but as it can be seen with many other encryption and anonymity services they can and are being actively used by criminal groups and organizations. The privacy they provide are actually being used with legitimate purpose but is often misused with malicious goals. Encrypted messaging apps therefore unintentionally create a safe haven for criminals to band together and plan criminal acts. This creates another challenge for law enforcement, as authorities must distinguish between legitimate private communication and criminal activity. Governments should therefore seek solutions that address the misuse of these platforms without unnecessarily weakening privacy protections for ordinary users. International cooperation may also help authorities respond to criminal activities that take place across different jurisdictions. )
